    <summary>Android log file analyzer with AI-assisted analysis</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[
LogTapper opens logcat, bugreport, dumpstate and kernel log captures, runs YAML-defined
processors over them, and exposes the results to AI agents over MCP.

Built for Android developers, IT staff and support personnel:

- Load logcat, bugreport, dumpstate and kernel (dmesg) captures, or stream live from ADB.
- Search, filter and run custom analysis pipelines powered by a YAML processor system
  with embedded Rhai scripting.
- Ships a bundled MCP server so AI agents (Claude Code, Claude Desktop and other MCP
  clients) get direct tool access to search lines, run pipelines, read state-tracker
  events, and manage bookmarks and watches -- no separate Node.js install needed.

This package installs LogTapper machine-wide under %ProgramFiles%\LogTapper, registers
the .lts / .ltw file associations, and pulls the Microsoft Edge WebView2 Runtime on
Windows 10 if it is missing.

LogTapper updates itself (Settings > General > Updates), so choco list --local-only can
report an older version than the running app. Run choco upgrade logtapper to reinstall
the current release and bring the two back in step.
    ]]></description>
